Title: Restore systemPreferences.isAeroGlassEnabled()
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

Deprecated in Electron 35 and removed in 36, on the grounds that it had returned
a constant `true` ever since v23 required Windows 10, where DWM composition
cannot be disabled. That reasoning does not apply to this build: it runs on
Windows 7, 8 and 8.1, where composition can be switched off, so the function
answers a real question again -- notably "will a transparent window work", which
is what callers used it for.

Nothing of Chromium's had to be restored for this. ui::win::IsAeroGlassEnabled
survives in ui/base/win/shell.h via chromium/ui/0162, which several patches in
this series already depend on; only Electron's binding to it was gone.

  shell/browser/api/electron_api_system_preferences.h
                          declares IsAeroGlassEnabled() in the existing IS_WIN
                          block.
  .../electron_api_system_preferences_win.cc
                          one-line implementation, plus the ui/base/win/shell.h
                          include it needs.
  .../electron_api_system_preferences.cc
                          registers "isAeroGlassEnabled" under its own
                          BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) guard. The nearby block is
                          IS_WIN || IS_MAC, which this cannot join: there is no
                          macOS implementation to bind.

  docs/api/system-preferences.md
                          the API reference entry. Not cosmetic -- package()
                          runs create-typescript-definitions over docs/, so this
                          entry is what puts isAeroGlassEnabled() into the
                          electron.d.ts that ships in the npm package. Without
                          it the method exists at runtime but not for
                          TypeScript. The example is deliberately simpler than
                          upstream's old one, which needed a @ts-expect-error
                          annotation pinned to a line number.

  docs/breaking-changes.md
                          notes on both entries -- the 35.0 deprecation and the
                          36.0 removal -- saying the function is restored here
                          and why. Left as notes so upstream's record of its own
                          decision stays intact.

  spec/ts-smoke/electron/main.ts
                          drops the `@ts-expect-error Removed API` above the
                          isAeroGlassEnabled() call, which the docs entry above
                          makes a lie: electron.d.ts declares the method again,
                          the call type-checks, and tsc fails the build with
                          TS2578 "Unused '@ts-expect-error' directive". Not a
                          test-only concern -- the npm_action that generates
                          electron.d.ts runs this type check, so the build stops
                          at //electron:build_electron_definitions. Now a
                          console.log of the result, matching the getColor line
                          above it.

